<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY - a comment ABOVE the root
        breaks `sf` deploy at conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent
        xml file" error.

        WS7 (2026-08-30). Per-field extraction confidence, e.g.
        {"noi":0.92,"year_built":0.4}. Machine-written by LLMExtractionParser at Lead
        creation via EmailToLeadService's existing insert - never hand-edited, and this
        field is never assigned FLS edit access to any human persona.

        NOT A LIST-VIEW-FILTERABLE SIGNAL, AND THAT IS WHY Low_Confidence_Field_Count__c
        EXISTS AS A SEPARATE FIELD (GATE D). A Long Text Area cannot be used in a list-view
        filter, a report filter, or a formula's CONTAINS(). Low_Confidence_Field_Count__c is
        the derived, filterable Number that drives the Review Queue list view; this field is
        the raw map that Low_Confidence_Field_Count__c is counted FROM. Do not attempt to
        reconstruct or duplicate that count from this field in a list view - it cannot be
        done here.

        NOT Parse_Confidence__c and NOT categoryConfidence. Parse_Confidence__c is a single
        HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW band over the whole-email is_acquisition_related question and feeds
        the existing Review_Queue filter unchanged. This field answers a different, narrower
        question - per-DEAL-FIELD confidence - which is why the Review Queue filter joins the
        two with OR rather than replacing one with the other.

        Malformed or absent per-field confidence from the model yields an empty map here,
        never a thrown exception - the inbound email pipeline must never be made to throw
        (see LLMExtractionParser's own "unexpected response shape yields an empty-but-valid
        result" contract).
    -->
    <fullName>Field_Confidence_JSON__c</fullName>
    <description>Per-field extraction confidence as a JSON map, e.g. {"noi":0.92,"year_built":0.4}. Written by LLMExtractionParser at Lead creation. Machine-written only, never hand-edited. Not filterable - the filterable signal derived from this map is Low_Confidence_Field_Count__c.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Raw per-field confidence JSON from the LLM extraction. Machine-written - do not hand-edit. Use Low_Confidence_Field_Count__c to filter or sort.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Field Confidence JSON</label>
    <length>32768</length>
    <trackFeedHistory>false</trackFeedHistory>
    <type>LongTextArea</type>
    <visibleLines>6</visibleLines>
</CustomField>
